# Rank 0's /health lists every rank's SSD store (`spill.ranks`, `spill.ranks_age_s`). Each rank keeps its own store on its
# own Spark and /health showed rank 0's only: on 2026-10-16 at 01:11, du read node1 27.29 GiB, node2 20.10 GiB, and the
# board showed one number. The memory guard's all-gather (MEMQ, both ranks) carries each rank's store beside its memory
# status: stored, written in all and disk free in MiB (the gather is int32), states, blocks, states written. A read that
# fails sends zeros, so every rank sends the same length and the all-gather cannot wait on a missing rank.

